{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++0x code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++0x code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cassert>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\n// Flattened matrix representation: size (k+1)*(k+1)\ntypedef vector<int> mt;\n\nint K; // global k for shift and multiplication\n\nmt shift(const mt &a, int shift)\n{\n    int k = K;\n    int n = k + 1;\n    shift = (k - shift) % k;\n    mt res = a;\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < k; ++j) {\n            res[i * n + j] = a[((i + shift) % k) * n + ((j + shift) % k)];\n        }\n    }\n    for (int j = 0; j < k; ++j) {\n        res[k * n + j] = a[k * n + ((j + shift) % k)];\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nmt operator *(const mt &a, const mt &b)\n{\n    int n = K + 1;\n    mt res(n * n, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int tmp = 0;\n            for (int l = 0; l < n; ++l) {\n                tmp = (tmp + 1ll * a[i * n + l] * b[l * n + j]) % MOD;\n            }\n            res[i * n + j] = tmp;\n        }\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n    ll n;\n    int k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    K = k;\n    int max_depth = 0;\n    {\n        ll tmp = n;\n        while (tmp != 0) {\n            ++max_depth;\n            tmp /= k;\n        }\n    }\n    vector<mt> dp(max_depth);\n    int sz = k + 1;\n    // dp[0]\n    dp[0].assign(sz * sz, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= k; ++j) {\n            dp[0][i * sz + j] = (i == j || j == 0);\n        }\n    }\n    mt e(sz * sz, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n        e[i * sz + i] = 1;\n    }\n    for (int depth = 1; depth < max_depth; ++depth) {\n        dp[depth] = e;\n        mt bs = dp[depth - 1];\n        int curx = k;\n        for (int i = 0; (1 << i) <= curx; ++i) {\n            if (curx & (1 << i)) {\n                dp[depth] = bs * shift(dp[depth], (1 << i));\n                curx ^= (1 << i);\n            }\n            bs = bs * shift(bs, (1 << i));\n        }\n    }\n    mt base(sz, 0);\n    base[k] = 1;\n    int sl = 0;\n    ll x = n;\n    vector<int> vec;\n    while (x != 0) {\n        vec.push_back(x % k);\n        x /= k;\n    }\n    int len = int(vec.size());\n    for (int cur_depth = len - 1; cur_depth >= 0; --cur_depth) {\n        int rest = vec[cur_depth];\n        for (int it = 0; it < rest; ++it, sl = (sl + 1) % k) {\n            // base is 1 x sz, shift returns sz x sz, result is 1 x sz\n            mt shifted = shift(dp[cur_depth], sl);\n            mt newbase(sz, 0);\n            for (int j = 0; j < sz; ++j) {\n                int tmp = 0;\n                for (int l = 0; l < sz; ++l) {\n                    tmp = (tmp + 1ll * base[l] * shifted[l * sz + j]) % MOD;\n                }\n                newbase[j] = tmp;\n            }\n            base = newbase;\n        }\n    }\n    int res = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n        res = (res + base[i]) % MOD;\n    }\n    cout << res << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model"